{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/740431-can-i-get-some-help-with-a-beast-concept","id":740431,"title":"Can I get some help with a beast concept...?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-29T18:27:50-07:00","id":740431,"title":"Can I get some help with a beast concept...?","content":"I'm not sure what to stat this as... (family/hungers/powers)... but I have an idea for a Beast that epitomizes the idea of the 'dark lord/lady' that rules with an iron fist/dread powers (and maybe a legion of terror? =P). Can I get some help in what would be the best fit?<br /> <br /> Note: I kinda see the character as someone who seeks out those who bully, lord over, or just generally abuse their power.. and shows them what its like to be under the foot of someone more powerful than them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T19:12:41-07:00","id":740570,"title":"","content":"I can see it as a Anakin,you could make a lair that is like this vast prison where those who abuse others are locked awayanaking have both super strenght and super intelligence,so you could make a lord that is not only sronger than others,but smarter than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T19:20:03-07:00","id":740587,"title":"","content":"Family wise the Anakim are probably what you're looking for.<br /> <br /> Pg 27 &quot;For all that they can express<br /> dominance by other means, the<br /> Anakim are creatures of force. Its<br /> use and abuse come naturally<br /> to them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hunger wise Tyrants (Pg 36) would be a good fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8983-a-gloomy-person","name":"A Gloomy Person","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8983_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T19:44:01-07:00","id":740656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/740431-can-i-get-some-help-with-a-beast-concept#post740431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what to stat this as... (family/hungers/powers)... but I have an idea for a Beast that epitomizes the idea of the 'dark lord/lady' that rules with an iron fist/dread powers (and maybe a legion of terror? =P). Can I get some help in what would be the best fit?<br /> <br /> Note: I kinda see the character as someone who seeks out those who bully, lord over, or just generally abuse their power.. and shows them what its like to be under the foot of someone more powerful than them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with <b>Gloomy Person</b> - the obvious choice is a Tyrant, a Beast who Hungers for Power. However, you could also go with a Nemesis - a Beast who Hungers to punish the wicked. You might even justify a Collector, who's Hunger drives them to collect the worst sinners they can find (I'd expect to see a Lair themed after a prison or Hell, in this situation)<br /> <br /> As for Family . . . the Anakim (Giants) are born from nightmares of powerlessness. They tower over their prey, and make them feel small, and weak, and helpless.<br /> <br /> But that's not the only option. If you're thinking Sauron, the Eye that towers over all, before which no one may hide . . . that sounds like an Ugallu. Born from nightmares where the dreamer is exposed, unable to find any shelter, Ugallu are often thought of as flying monsters. But you could also picture one standing atop a great peak, glaring down at the world . . .<br /> <br /> Also pretty sure the Kickstarter draft provided an example of a Namtaru (nightmare of revulsion/hideousness), who specialized in feeding on people who were beautiful on the outside, but who were ugly/wicked/evil on the inside. But if you want a legion of terror, I think I'd go with Anakim or Ugallu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 10-29-2015, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T05:47:15-07:00","id":741447,"title":"","content":"Any of the Families will work for the concept - there are two mechanical aspects of Family, being Birthright and one of your starting Atavisms. Wait, no, not everyone. Eshmaki are pretty much stealthy characters, and that doesn't quite fit the concept. However, everyone but Eshmaki have two potential Atavism that works with the Dark Queen concept (Looming Presence, Alien Allure, Shadowed Soul, Eye of Heaven, Mirmir's Wisdom, Needs Must, Siren's Treacherous Song, Unbreakable), though the Namtaru two are a bit lackluster. Meanwhile, the Birthrights don't really interact with your concept at all. Giants break through barriers, Maraka inflict a minor Physical penalty, Namtaru effectively lowers a target's Composure for a scene, and Ugallu can find something hidden. I know others have been suggesting Giants, but the only part of the Giant that directly impacts the whole Dark Queen concept are the two suggested Atavisms, and there's no reason you can't get them fairly quickly in play.<br /> <br /> For Hunger, Tyrant is the most obvious (especially with the bullying angle), but Hungers are highly flexible and, given your admitted aspiration to raise a collection of supernaturals, likely have access to Family Dinner on a regular basis. So, you really could go with almost any of them. Collector is another one that works. When combining either of the two with Needs Must, you also gain the ability to sense new and perfect canidates to recruit into your growing Dark Army. Honestly, the Hungers are so flexible that we can fit your &quot;collect members&quot; ambition into three different ones and not change how you feed your Satiety at all. I wouldn't put too much worry into it.<br /> <br /> For the Dark Queen concept, you generally want more social abilities. I rattled off a few Atavisms earlier, but to be honest? The best abilities when interacting with other supernaturals come from maintaining High Satiety, including Mother's Kiss and other innate abilities. So you're going to want to look at Nightmares, which also rely on High Satiety. Behold My True Form and You Must Obey are always two very good ones to have. Run Away and You Cannot Run are two favorites of mine when it comes to combat control effects, and The Void is Waiting is a good anti-supernatural effect for keeping the minions in line, especially given the effects of the High Satiety Condition. Fear is Contageous, You Can't Wake Up and You Are Infected are all &quot;metamagic&quot; abilities if you spend a lot of time using Nightmares.<br /> <br /> You Are Alone and We Know All Your Secrets are very good for Social Maneuvering when it comes to manipulating Doors, which actually work well with Looming Presence and Alien Allure. You can use any Nightmare as Hard Leverage, WKAYS has an additional Door-removal abilities at High Satiety, LP removes an additional door when you Hard Leverage (automatic with any Nightmare use), for a total of automatically 3 doors removed before rolling. Meanwhile, AA ensures a baseline of Good Impression while YAA pushes that up to Excellent, if not higher, ensuring likability. Considering that recruitment is going to be a Social Maneuver, this combination helps break down barriers in a single sitting instead of waiting days. The maximum number of doors one can usually have is 9, which requires 5 in Resolve and Composure*, acting in opposition to character's Virtue, and involve a breaking point. With Fast Talking 4 and Advanced Striking Looks + AA, we're looking at opening 6 doors with a single roll and an hour between rolls, plus potentially lowering the doors required by 1. <br /> <br /> *Yes, I know that its possible to go above Resolve/Composure 5, but if we're talking 6+ beings, your Nightmares likely won't work either, so its going to be a lot harder no matter the case.<br /> <br /> So, that should cover everything central to the concept. You'll have to work out how you want to build up the Lair, or focus on more occult aspects, or just buy up dots in Allies and Status for the rest. Good luck!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T15:23:57-08:00","id":750219,"title":"","content":"Thank you all very much! I will definatly keep all the advise in mind when I find a game to get in on =D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}